  "sections": [
    {
      "h2": "Your rights under EU rules",
      "html": "<ul><li><strong>Roam like at home</strong>: use your EU mobile plan in other EU/EEA countries at no extra charge, subject to fair use. The rules run until 2032.</li><li><strong>Contract length</strong>: the initial commitment of a consumer contract can’t exceed 24 months.</li><li><strong>Contract summary</strong>: providers must give you a short summary of the main terms before you sign.</li><li><strong>Number porting</strong>: your number should move within one working day of the agreed date.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "h2": "Country snapshots",
      "html": "<p><strong>Germany</strong>: Telekom, Vodafone, O2 Telefónica and 1&amp;1, with cable, DSL and expanding fibre. <strong>France</strong>: Orange, SFR, Bouygues Telecom and Free compete hard on fibre “box” bundles. <strong>Spain</strong>: one of Europe’s most fibre-rich countries, with Movistar, MasOrange, Vodafone and DIGI. <strong>Italy</strong>: TIM, Iliad, WindTre and Fastweb + Vodafone. <strong>Netherlands</strong>: KPN, VodafoneZiggo and Odido. <strong>Ireland</strong>: eir, Vodafone, Three and Virgin Media.</p>"
    },
    {
      "h2": "Moving to or within Europe",
      "html": "<ul><li>You may need a local address, ID and bank account to sign a contract; prepaid SIMs are simpler but may need ID registration.</li><li>Fibre installs can take weeks in some countries. Order early.</li><li>Each country has a telecoms regulator that publishes coverage maps and complaint routes.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "h2": "Visiting from the UK",
      "html": "<p>Since Brexit, UK mobile plans aren’t covered by EU roaming rules. Many UK networks charge a daily fee in Europe or include roaming only on certain plans. Check before you travel. See our <a href=\"/roaming/\">roaming guide</a>.</p>"
    }
  ],
  "faqs": [
    {
      "q": "Do EU roaming rules apply to UK SIMs?",
      "a": "No. The UK left the EU roaming scheme. Some UK plans still include EU roaming, but many charge a daily fee."
    },
    {
      "q": "Can I use an EU SIM permanently in another EU country?",
      "a": "Roam like at home is designed for periodic travel. Operators can apply fair use limits if you mainly use your SIM abroad for a long period."
    }
  ],
